 (0..101 bar(g))?? Wait — look at page 4 header: \"Qmin\" columns with \"0..101 bar(g)\" and \"4..101 bar(g)\", rows \"MR 1:30\" and \"MR 1:50\". Hmm:\n\nPage 4 header:\n- Main characteristics: Type, DN body, DN cartr., G-value\n- Essential characteristics: Qmax, Qt, Qmin (colspan 2)\n- Conditional parts: Number of drums, Control element\n- Essential parts: Blade angle, Blade qty, Bearing dimensions (colspan 4? Actually 6)\n\nRow 2: Qmin sub-columns: \"0..101 bar(g)\" and \"4..101 bar(g)\" (colspan 4 total covering both).\nRow 3: \"MR 1:30\" and \"MR 1:50\".\n\nSo for the continuation table, Qmin MR 1:30 applies 0..101 bar(g), and Qmin MR 1:50 applies 4..101 bar(g). Interesting — different pressure conditions from table 1 (page 3) where MR 1:30 was 3...101 bar(g) and MR 1:50 was 8...101 bar(g).\n\nThis is complex. The best approach: preserve the tables as matrix_tables with rows, and populate model_level characteristics.\n\nThe rows are grouped by (Type, DN body, DN cartr.) with 3 G-values each. Each G-value row has different Qmax/Qt/Qmin/drums/blade angle/blade qty.\n\nHow to model model_family models? The natural model identity: type + G-value + pressure range? The \"family\" is defined by G-value and meter class (MR ratio 1:20, 1:30, 1:50). Actually in gas meters, the \"meter class\" (MR = rangeability) determines Qmin: Qmax/20, Qmax/30, Qmax/50. And the G-value (G100, G160...) determines Qmax.\n\nGiven the complexity, I think the cleanest extraction:\n\n1. matrix_tables: two entries (Table 1 - page 3; Table 2 - continuation page 4), with flattened rows preserving all columns.\n\n2. model_family.models: one per unique model variant. What's the model id? Perhaps \"FMT-Lx DN50 G100\" etc. That's a lot of models. Let me enumerate.\n\nPage 3 Table 1 rows (each block of 3 rows shares Type/DN body/DN cartr./drums/control/blade qty/bearings):\n\nBlock A: Type \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", DN body 50, DN cartr. 80:\n- G100: Qmax 160, Qt 32, Qmin: MR1:20=8, MR1:30=5, MR1:50=3; drums 7/1, control 0,02; blade angle 55, blade qty 12; bearings std front 3x6x3, rear 2x5x2, optional front 3x8x4, rear 3x6x3\n- G160: Qmax 250, Qt 50, Qmin: 12.5/8/5; blade angle 45, qty 14\n- G250: Qmax 400, Qt 80, Qmin: 20/12.5/8; blade angle 35, qty 16\n\nBlock B: Type \"FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", DN body 80, DN cartr. 80:\n- G100: Qmax 160, Qt 32, Qmin 8/5/3; drums 7/1; control 0,02; blade 55/12; bearings 3x6x3, 2x5x2, 3x8x4, 3x6x3\n- G160: Qmax 250, Qt 50, Qmin 12.5/8/5; blade 45/14\n- G250: Qmax 400, Qt 80, Qmin 20/12.5/8; blade 35/16\n\nBlock C: Type \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", DN 80/100:\n- G160: Qmax 250, Qt 50, Qmin 12.5/8/5; blade 55/12; bearings 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 5x10x3, 3x6x3\n- G250: Qmax 400, Qt 80, Qmin 20/12.5/8; blade 45/14\n- G400: Qmax 650, Qt 130, Qmin 32.5/20/12.5; blade 35/16\n\nBlock D: Type \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", DN 100/80:\n- G100: 160/32; Qmin 8/5/3; blade 55/12; bearings 3x6x3, 2x5x2, 3x8x4, 3x6x3\n- G160: 250/50; 12.5/8/5; 45/14\n- G250: 400/80; 20/12.5/8; 35/16\n\nBlock E: Type \"FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", DN 100/100:\n- G160: 250/50; 12.5/8/5; 55/12; bearings 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 5x10x3, 3x6x3\n- G250: 400/80; 20/12.5/8; 45/14\n- G400: 650/130; 32.5/20/12.5; 35/16\n\nBlock F: Type \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", DN 100/150:\n- G400: Qmax 650, Qt 130, Qmin 32.5 (MR1:20), 20 (MR1:30), 12.5 (MR1:50); drums 7/1, control 0,02; blade 55/12; bearings 5x11x5, 5x11x5, 5x16x5, 5x11x5\n- G650: 1000/200; 50/32/20; blade 45/14\n- G1000: 1600/320; 80/50/32; drums 8/0, control 0,2; blade 35/16\n\nBlock G: FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, DN 150/100:\n- G160: 250/50; 12.5/8/5; 55/12; bearings 3x8x4, 3x6x3, 5x10x3, 3x6x3\n- G250: 400/80; 20/12.5/8; 45/14\n- G400: 650/130; 32.5/20/12.5; 35/16\n\nBlock H: FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, DN 150/150:\n- G400: 650/130; 32.5/20/12.5; drums 7/1 control 0,02; blade 55/12; bearings 5x11x5 ×2, 5x16x5, 5x11x5\n- G650: 1000/200; 50/32/20; 45/14\n- G1000: 1600/320; 80/50/32; drums 8/0 control 0,2; 35/16\n\nBlock I: FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, DN 150/200: