00/500 G10000\n64. FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN500/400 G2500\n65. FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN500/400 G4000\n66. FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN500/400 G6500\n67. FMT-S/FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN500/500 G4000\n68. FMT-S/FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN500/500 G6500\n69. FMT-S/FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN500/500 G10000\n70. FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN500/600 G6500\n71. FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN500/600 G10000\n72. FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN500/600 G16000\n73. FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN600/500 G4000\n74. FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN600/500 G6500\n75. FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN600/500 G10000\n76. FMT-S/FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN600/600 G6500\n77. FMT-S/FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN600/600 G10000\n78. FMT-S/FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN600/600 G16000\n\nWait, page 4 blocks: M (200/250), N (250/250 FMT-S...), O (250/300), P (300/250), Q (300/300 FMT-S...), R (300/400), S (400/400 FMT-S...), T (400/500), U (500/400), V (500/500 FMT-S...), W (500/600), X (600/500), Y (600/600 FMT-S...). That's 13 blocks × 3 = 39 rows. Total 36+39 = 75 rows. My list above: items 37-75 = 39. Good, 75 total.\n\nThat's a LOT of model entries and model_level values (75×2 = 150 structured objects). Plus matrix tables with 75 rows × 17 fields. The JSON will be big (~50-70KB). Doable but risky for length limits. Let me consider trimming: do I need both full matrix rows AND model_level AND models[]? The schema's R137 example includes all three (models[], matrix_tables, model_level for qmax/qt/qmin). I'll follow but maybe restrict model_level to qmax and qt (skip g_value since in model_id; skip qmin due to config axis, covered in tables).\n\nActually, to control size, maybe I can drop model_family.models entries' attributes entirely and keep model_level with qmax/qt. And keep matrix tables complete. That is: 75 model_ids (~75 lines short), 150 model_level values, 75 matrix rows. It's large but let's do it. Estimated tokens: each model_level value ~ {\"model\": \"...\", \"value\": N} ~ 15 tokens → 150×15 = 2250 tokens. Model ids ~10 tokens each ×75 = 750. Matrix rows: each row ~ 60-80 tokens × 75 = 5000-6000 tokens. Total ~ 9-10K tokens for data + overhead. Acceptable (~15K output). Let me be careful and systematic.\n\nActually, wait. Should I really include the full bearing dims etc. in matrix rows? Yes — fidelity.\n\nLet me now also decide: For page-3 table, is Qmin MR1:20 always = Qmax/20? Check G400 block F: Qmax 650, qmins 32.5/20/12.5 → 650/20=32.5 ✓. G1000: 1600 → 80/50/32 ✓ (1600/50=32). G1600: 2500 → 125/80/50 ✓. Page 4 G2500: 4000 → 1:30: 133 (4000/30=133.3), 1:50: 80 ✓. G4000: 6500 → 216/130 ✓ (6500/30=216.7, /50=130). G10000: 16000 → 533/320 ✓. G16000: 25000 → 800/400? 25000/30 = 833, hmm 800 listed. 25000/31≈806. Eh, printed values stand. G6500: 10000 → 333/200 ✓ (10000/30=333.3, /50=200). OK.\n\nNow assemble matrix table rows.\n\nTable 1 (page 3) rows — flattened. I'll write model column as \"type\" string as given, e.g. \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", \"FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\". In rows object keys: type, dn_body, dn_cartridge, g_value, qmax, qt, qmin_mr_1_20, qmin_mr_1_30, qmin_mr_1_50, drums, control_element, blade_angle, blade_qty, bearing_front_standard, bearing_rear_standard, bearing_front_optional, bearing_rear_optional.\n\nColumn units: [null, \"mm\", \"mm\", null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null, \"m³/h\", \"degree\", null, \"mm\", \"mm\", \"mm\", \"mm\"]. For bearings \"mm\" is per dimension; it's a triplet string \"3x6x3\". Fine.\n\nDecimals: 12,5 → 12.5; 32,5 → 32.5; 0,02 → 0.02; 0,2 → 0.2.\n\nRows:\n\nA (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 50, 80):\n1. G100: 160, 32, 8, 5, 3, \"7/1\", 0.02, 55, 12, \"3x6x3\", \"2x5x2\", \"3x8x4\", \"3x6x3\"\n2. G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, \"7/1\", 0.02, 45, 14, same bearings\n3. G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, \"7/1\", 0.02, 35, 16, same\n\nB (FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 80, 80):\n4. G100: 160, 32, 8, 5, 3, \"7/1\", 0.02, 55, 12, \"3x6x3\",\"2x5x2\",\"3x8x4\",\"3x6x3\"\n5. G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, ..., 45, 14\n6. G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, ..., 35, 16\n\nC (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 80, 100):\n7. G160: 250, 50, 12.5, 8, 5, 55, 12, \"3x8x4\",\"3x6x3\",\"5x10x3\",\"3x6x3\"\n8. G250: 400, 80, 20, 12.5, 8, 45, 14\n9. G400: 650, 130, 32.5, 20, 12.5, 35, 16\n\nD (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 100, 80):\n10. G100: 160, 32, 8,5,3, 55,12, \"3x6x3\",\"2x5x2\",\"3x8x4\",\"3x6x3\"\n11. G160: 250,50,12.5,8,5, 45,14\n12. G250: 400,80,20,12.5,8, 35,16\n\nE (FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 100, 100):\n13. G160: 250,50,12.5,8,5, 55,12, \"3x8x4\",\"3x6x3\",\"5x10x3\",\"3x6x3\"\n14. G250: 400,80,20,12.5,8, 45,14\n15. G400: 650,130,32.5,20,12.5, 35,16\n\nF (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 100, 150):\n16. G400: 650,130,32.5,20,12.5, \"7/1\",0.02,55,12, \"5x11x5\",\"5x11x5\",\"5x16x5\",\"5x11x5\"\n17. G650: 1000,200,50,32,20, \"7/1\",0.02,45,14\n18. G1000: 1600,320,80,50,32, \"8/0\",0.2,35,16\n\nG (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 150, 100):\n19. G160: 250,50,12.5,8,5, 55,12, \"3x8x4\",\"3x6x3\",\"5x10x3\",\"3x6x3\"\n20. G250: 400,80,20,12.5,8, 45,14\n21. G400: 650,130,32.5,20,12.5, 35,16\n\nH (FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 150, 150):\n22. G400: 650,130,32.5,20,12.5, 55,12, \"5x11x5\",\"5x11x5\",\"5x16x5\",\"5x11x5\"\n23. G650: 1000,200,50,32,20, 45,14\n24. G1000: 1600,320,80,50,32, \"8/0\",0.2,35,16\n\nI (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 150, 200):\n25. G650: 1000,200,50,32,20, \"7/1\",0.02,55,12, \"5x16x5\",\"5x16x5\",\"8x22x7\",\"5x16x5\"\n26. G1000: 1600,320,80,50,32, \"8/0\",0.2,45,14\n27. G1600: 2500,500,125,80,50, \"8/0\",0.2,35,16\n\nJ (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 200, 150):\n28. G400: 650,130,32.5,20,12.5, 55,12, \"5x11x5\",\"5x11x5\",\"5x16x5\",\"5x11x5\"\n29. G650: 1000,200,50,32,20, 45,14\n30. G1000: 1600,320,80,50,32, \"8/0\",0.2,35,16\n\nK (FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 200, 200):\n31. G650: 1000,200,50,32,20, \"7/1\",0.02,55,12, \"5x16x5\",\"5x16x5\",\"8x22x7\",\"5x16x5\"\n32. G1000: 1600,320,80,50,32, \"8/0\",0.2,45,14\n33. G1600: 2500,500,125,80,50, \"8/0\",0.2,35,16\n\nL (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc, 250, 200):\n34. G650: 1000,200,50,32,20, 55,12, \"5x16x5\",\"5x16x5\",\"8x22x7\",\"5x16x5\"\n35. G1000: 1600,320,80,50,32, \"8/0\",0.2,45,14\n36. G1600: 2500,500,125,80,50, \"8/0\",0.2,35,16\n\nTable 2 (page 4). Colu