min_mr_1_20\", \"qmin_mr_1_30\", \"qmin_mr_1_50\", \"drums_before_and_after_comma\", \"control_element\", \"blade_angle\", \"blade_qty\", \"bearing_standard_front\", \"bearing_standard_rear\", \"bearing_optional_front\", \"bearing_optional_rear\"]\n\ncolumn_units: [null, \"mm\", \"mm\", null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null, \"m³/h\", \"degree\", null, \"mm\", \"mm\", \"mm\", \"mm\"]\n\ndescription: \"Qmin applicability by meter ratio (MR): MR 1:20 for 0-101 bar(g), MR 1:30 for 3-101 bar(g), MR 1:50 for 8-101 bar(g). Standard bearings applicable 0-101 bar(g); optional bearings 3-101 bar(g). Bearing dimensions: inside diameter x outside diameter x width in mm. Control element value in m³/h.\"\n\nTable 2 columns:\n[\"type\", \"dn_body\", \"dn_cartridge\", \"g_value\", \"qmax\", \"qt\", \"qmin_mr_1_30\", \"qmin_mr_1_50\", \"drums_before_and_after_comma\", \"control_element\", \"blade_angle\", \"blade_qty\", \"bearing_standard_front\", \"bearing_standard_rear\", \"bearing_optional_front\", \"bearing_optional_rear\"]\n\ncolumn_units: [null, \"mm\", \"mm\", null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null, \"m³/h\", \"degree\", null, \"mm\", \"mm\", \"mm\", \"mm\"]\n\ndescription: \"Qmin applicability: MR 1:30 for 0-101 bar(g), MR 1:50 for 4-101 bar(g). Bearings applicable 0-101 bar(g).\"\n\nNow rows. To save space I'll write each row object on one line.\n\nBlade angle \"45 / 30\": I'll write \"45/30\".\n\nDrums \"7 / 1\" → \"7/1\"; \"8 / 0\" → \"8/0\".\n\nControl element: 0.02, 0.2 numbers.\n\nNow model_level arrays:\n\nqmax values: for each of the 75 models. And qt values: 75.\n\nLet me tabulate qmax/qt per model id (already listed above).\n\n1 FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN50/80 G100: 160/32\n2 ... G160: 250/50\n3 ... G250: 400/80\n4 FMT-L/FMT-S/FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN80/80 G100: 160/32\n5 G160: 250/50\n6 G250: 400/80\n7 FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN80/100 G160: 250/50\n8 G250: 400/80\n9 G400: 650/130\n10 FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc DN100/80 G100: 160/32\n11 G160: 250/50\n12 G250: 400/80\n13