trol element (\"m³/h\"). So control element unit m³/h per the OCR. Odd (should be m³ probably) but keep as printed.\n\nLet me now also fill type_level values with footnote_markers: [] or omit? Rule: footnote_markers in shape; empty array fine. I'll include \"footnote_markers\": [] for completeness? The strict shape includes it. I'll include empty arrays. Actually to reduce size, include them — values objects need the shape. I'll include.\n\nUnit ids: leave null.\n\nLet me now also decide: \"maximum_operating_pressure\" — include as type_level with value 101 bar(g). The header says \"0..101 bar(g)\" for MR1:20 Qmin and standard bearings; other configs 3/4/8..101. So 101 is the common max. I'll include:\n\"maximum_operating_pressure\": {\"value\": 101, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar(g)\", \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n\nReasonable.\n\nAlso \"destined for measurement\": attribute name \"measured_quantity\"? I'll use \"measurement_quantity\"? Canonical label — \"destined_for_measurement_of\"? I'll use \"measured_medium\": \"Gas volume\". Choose \"measured_quantity\": value \"Gas volume\". Fine.\n\nNow the components section final:\n\n\"components\": [\n  {\n    \"role\": \"mechanical index (interchangeable component)\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"reed contact\", \"Wiegand\", \"encoder\"],\n    \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n    \"characteristics\": {\n      \"equipped_with\": {\"value\": \"reed contact, Wiegand or encoder\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"flow straightener (inlet)\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"10466/6-03\", \"10466/7-05\"],\n    \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n    \"characteristics\": {\n      \"applicability\": {\"value\": \"FMT-L: two different flow straighteners; FMT-S: large flow straightener only; FMT-Lx/FMT-Dc: inlet flow straightener identical to FMT-S\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nHmm, type_designations for straightener are doc numbers, not type designations. Slightly off but acceptable; alternatively empty and put doc numbers in characteristics. I'll keep doc numbers in type_designations with a characteristics note \"documentation_numbers\"? Redundant. Let me do: type_designations: [], characteristics: {\"documentation_numbers\": {value: \"10466/6-03, 10466/7-05\"...}, \"variants\": {value: \"large (1xDN inlet) / small (5xDN inlet)\"...}}. And note FMT-S uses large only. That's cleaner. Actually I have config_level for pipe lengths. Keep component simple.\n\nFinal components:\n\n[\n  {\n    \"role\": \"mechanical index (interchangeable component)\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"reed contact\", \"Wiegand\", \"encoder\"],\n    \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n    \"characteristics\": {}\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"inlet flow straightener\",\n    \"type_designations\": [],\n    \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n    \"characteristics\": {\n      \"documentation_numbers\": {\"value\": \"10466/6-03 and 10466/7-05\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []},\n      \"applicability\": {\"value\": \"FMT-L: two variants; FMT-S: large straightener only; FMT-Lx and FMT-Dc: identical to FMT-S\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nHmm, \"type_designations\": [\"reed contact\", \"Wiegand\", \"encoder\"] — these are output types, not designations. But with alternatives \"OR\" it conveys the options. Alternatively type_designations: [] and characteristics.pulse_equipment. I'll go with listing them as designations since they're the alternative configurations named in the cert. OK.\n\nconfig_level:\n\n[\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"straight_inlet_pipe_length\",\n    \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\",\n    \"axis\": \"meter model / installed flow straightener\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"condition\": \"FMT-L with large flow straightener\", \"value\": 1, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"FMT-L with small flow straightener\", \"value\": 5, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"FMT-S with large flow straightener\", \"value\": 1, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"FMT-Lx (no straight inlet tubing requirement)\", \"value\": 0, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"FMT-Dc (two FMT-Lx cartridges, same as FMT-Lx)\", \"value\": 0, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"}\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\nNow, certificate-level \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\".\n\nissuing_authority.name: \"NMi Certin B.V. (OIML Issuing Authority NL1)\"? Keep name \"NMi Certin B.V.\" and oiml_issuer_id \"NL1\".\n\nperson_title: not given → omit.\n\nLet me also reconsider \"certified_type.category\": \"Gas meter\". The doc says \"turbine gas meter\". Category options list includes \"Gas meter\". Use \"Gas meter\". description: \"Turbine gas meter for the measurement of gas volume\". Just \"Turbine gas meter\".\n\nAlso should I include accuracy class in certified_type? Not in schema; it's in recommendation.accuracy_classes. OK.\n\nEdge: The certificate says types \"FMT-L, FMT-S, FMT-Lx and FMT-Dc\". type_designations array: [\"FMT-L\", \"FMT-S\", \"FMT-Lx\", \"FMT-Dc\"].\n\nNow writing the full JSON. Be careful with \"m³/h\" superscript char — fine in JSON.\n\nAlso \"bar(g)\" as unit symbol — keep raw.\n\nDouble-check test report dates → ISO: 15 September 2014 → 2014-09-15; 18 December 2014 → 2014-12-18; 23 December 2014 → 2014-12-23; 28 January 2015 → 2015-01-28; 26 April 2018 → 2018-04-26.\n\nNow produce the final JSON. Let me be meticulous with the matrix rows.\n\nTable 1 rows (36):\n\nRow1: type \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", dn_body 50, dn_cartridge 80, g_value 100, qmax 160, qt 32, qmin_mr_1_20 8, qmin_mr_1_30 5, qmin_mr_1_50 3, drums \"7/1\", control_element 0.02, blade_angle 55, blade_qty 12, bsf \"3x6x3\", bsr \"2x5x2\", bof \"3x8x4\", bor \"3x6x3\"\nRow2: g 160, qmax 250, qt 50, qmin 12.5/8/5, 45, 14, same bearings\nRow3: g 250, 400, 80, 20/12.5/8, 35, 16, same bearings\nRow4: type \"FMT-L, FMT-S, FM